% ============================================================================
% Headline 1: Governance conflict error predicate  [EXERCISED 2026-07-28 + 2026-08-03, check -k]
% ============================================================================
% Fires when a credential carries all three governance mandates -- eIDAS
% mandate, privacy requirement, and VCDM-conformance mandate -- and no single
% format satisfies them jointly. Gating on all three annotations (D-039,
% 2026-07-28) makes the triple conjunction minimal: dropping any one mandate
% removes a precondition, so every proper subset (G0-G6) is satisfiable and
% only the full conjunction (G7) is UNSAT.
%
% Status (exercised 2026-07-28 full battery and 2026-08-03 G0-G7 re-run with
% refinery-cli check -k, image digest
% sha256:88f1332e9aae356d91aef86aaaa3368be1b3931929fb3e10d87d65ab8a7fca8e):
%   - csok.problem / csok_2x.problem / csok_3x.problem -> "Inconsistencies
%     found in model: governance_conflict::governance_conflict(IncomeCred,
%     income_format): error." (one atom per income credential at 2x/3x).
%   - evaluation/instances/sensitivity_G0..G6.problem -> "Model is consistent"
%     (SAT). Per the 2026-08-03 re-run all eight instances import this
%     predicate, so the seven SAT verdicts hold with the predicate loaded:
%     it cannot fire on any proper subset of the three mandates.
%   - evaluation/instances/sensitivity_G7.problem -> "Inconsistencies found in
%     model: governance_conflict::governance_conflict(cred_3, fmt_3): error."
%   Verbatim verdict tables: vault A-004 constraint-sensitivity-variants.
%
% The three clauses partition the failure condition
%   !(conforms_vcdm(f) & supports_predicate_proof(f)):
%   Clause 1: VCDM-conformant, but no predicate proofs (SD-JWT-VC, JSON-LD, JWT-VC).
%   Clause 2: predicate-proof-capable, but not VCDM-conformant (AnonCreds).
%   Clause 3: neither VCDM-conformant nor predicate-proof-capable (mdoc).
% No deployed format is both, so every format triggers a clause -> UNSAT.
% (Disjointness of the two capability sets alone does NOT imply coverage:
% clause 3 is required, otherwise mdoc escapes both clauses 1 and 2.)

import vc_metamodel.

error governance_conflict(Credential c, Formatted_Credential f) <->
    EidasMandate::target(_, c),
    PrivacyRequirement::target(_, c),
    VcdmConformance::target(_, c),
    format(c, f),
    conforms_vcdm(f),
    !supports_predicate_proof(f)
  ;
    EidasMandate::target(_, c),
    PrivacyRequirement::target(_, c),
    VcdmConformance::target(_, c),
    format(c, f),
    supports_predicate_proof(f),
    !conforms_vcdm(f)
  ;
    EidasMandate::target(_, c),
    PrivacyRequirement::target(_, c),
    VcdmConformance::target(_, c),
    format(c, f),
    !conforms_vcdm(f),
    !supports_predicate_proof(f).
